
Usage: /EXIT [<channel-name>|ALL|.]
  This command allows you to exit from a channel.  If this is the only
  channel you are in and the environment variable CHANNELLINGER is set
  to  N,  you  will  exit MTalk (ie., /QUIT).  If no <channel-name> is
  specified,  the current channel is assumed.  ALL exits all channels,
  and "." exits the current one.

  Example:
    /EXIT
    /EXIT bar

  See Also:
    /ENTER
    /SETENV CHANNELLINGER

